# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (de-bridged 2026-08-17, VICE wave #7, the last) ----
# VICE 3.10.0's x64sc runs ON THE HOST, headless: no QEMU, no guest Debian, no
# X server, no kiosk. Frames VICE_SHM_PATH -> SH_CAPTURE=shm; keys the vicectl
# socket + the ONE shared keysym table (VICE resolves keysym -> matrix through
# C64/gtk3_sym.vkm, the same file the bridged kiosk used); audio -sounddev wav
# -> named FIFO with the daemon as clock. Launcher: the shared
# stations/vice-native/x11-runtime.sh, VICE_NATIVE_* knobs.
# Build: scripts/build-guests/emulators/build-vice-native.sh c64.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Commodore 64 on the GEOS 2.0 deskTop — the disk window open on the System disk, its icons and menu bar drawn in GEOS's grey/white, with GEOS's own clock running — restored from a checkpoint by host-native VICE 3.10.0 x64sc with TRUE DRIVE emulation on drive 8. PUBLISHED SURFACE 768x544, MEASURED off the shm mapping (1 671 232 B = 64 + 768*544*4) — VICE has no MAME_SHM_SIZE equivalent, the surface IS the emulated screen times VICIIDoubleSize, so this geometry follows from VICE_NATIVE_ARGS and nothing else. THE ONLY IN-APPLICATION SCENE IN THE VICE WAVE: every other station's exhibit is an untouched cold boot that a relaunch reproduces for free, while this one is ~90 s of emulated true-drive loading away from the power-on screen, which is why this is the station that actually needed the checkpoint plane to work. KEYBOARD-ONLY for now — the bridged station had a COMM 1351 proportional mouse on control port 1 and the host-native input path has no pointer verb yet; see the note below. SID sound -> FIFO.
VICE_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/c64/vice-native/bin/x64sc
VICE_NATIVE_DATA=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/c64/vice-native/share/vice
# The ONLY thing that decides the published geometry (see SH_FIXTURE_DESC).
# -drive8truedrive is NOT optional: GEOS drives the 1541 itself and hangs under
# VICE's fast-loader shortcut. -autostart-handle-tde keeps true drive on across
# an autostart, which matters when the golden is BAKED and not when it is
# restored, and is kept so the bake path and the serve path are one command
# line. `-8` puts the same disk back under the head: a snapshot stores the
# drive's STATE but not its MEDIA, so without it the restored GEOS comes back to
# an empty drive. Unlike the C128's CP/M disk this one does NOT autoboot, so it
# rides on the command line rather than through VICE_NATIVE_ATTACH8.
VICE_NATIVE_ARGS=-drive8truedrive -autostart-handle-tde -VICIIdsize -8 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/c64/vice-native/media/GEOS-1351.D64
SH_VICECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64/ctl.sock
SH_VICESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64/us-layout.keysyms
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64/audio.fifo

# ---- THE POINTER IS NOT WIRED YET, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE ----
# The bridged exhibit translated the browser's absolute coordinates into PS/2
# relative motion for VICE's host-mouse boundary, and VICE turned that into the
# 1351's POT lines. The host-native path has no pointer verb AT ALL — not in
# vice_sock.rs (try_pointer_abs rejects the record and logs once) and not in
# vicectl — so the mouse is two new verbs plus the absolute-to-relative decision
# the keyboard path never had to make, i.e. a scoped piece of work rather than a
# knob. Converting keyboard-only is what ships the station today; the deskTop is
# still the scene, GEOS still runs, and the registry declares pointer.present
# false so the SPA offers no mouse affordance it cannot honour.

# ---- CHECKPOINT: ON, and this station is why the restore bug had to be FIXED ----
# Four of the five stations converted before this one shipped
# VICE_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=0 and cold-boot on reset, which cost them nothing
# because their scenes ARE cold boots. That fallback does not exist here. The
# restore was therefore tested before any of this was written: a golden baked
# through the monitor's own `dump`, restored in a FRESH process, comes back
# 768x544 with the deskTop pixel-correct and GEOS's own on-screen clock still
# advancing — the machine is alive, not merely painted.
# A checkpoint belongs to ONE machine type and ONE VICE build, so a rebuild
# rebakes.

# ---- STANDBY (instant-ready: an emulator nobody watches costs ~0 CPU) ----
# The launcher freezes the emulator once the scene has painted; the daemon owns
# it after that (SIGSTOP after the idle grace with zero sessions, unconditional
# SIGCONT the moment a visitor connects). WITHOUT THESE TWO LINES A DE-BRIDGED
# STATION BURNS A FULL CORE AROUND THE CLOCK. _PROC_MATCH is the anti-footgun:
# the signal only ever reaches a pid whose cmdline carries THIS station's own
# asset path. Rollback is one line: SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=0.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64/vice.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/c64/vice-native
VICE_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING ----
# 60/60, the VICE wave's floor, applied fleet-wide on 2026-08-17. The 80/80 the
# wave shipped on came from the vic20 bisect against THIS engine; that bisect
# was RE-RUN with realistic OVERLAPPING bursts once the exclusive-scan deadlock
# was fixed, and 60/60 was clean 12 of 12 while 40/40 corrupted 6 of 12. 60/60
# is one clear step above the last pacing observed to fail and is 28 % more
# throughput than 80/80. Verified on this station through the REAL SPA in a
# real browser, not just the control socket.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=60
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=60
# No SH_KEY_MAP and no per-station keymap file: VICE's own symbolic keymap does
# that job.
